pedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":3,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"15709560":["The Dream is a painting by Édouard Detaille created in 1888. It won the gold medal at the Salon in 1888.","The Dream (Detaille)"],"19912340":["The Defense of Champigny is a late-19th-century painting by Édouard Detaille. The painting, done in oil on canvas, depicts the Battle of Villiers during the Franco-Prussian War.","The Defense of Champigny"],"20441420":["Vive L'Empereur! is a history painting made retrospectively by French artist Édouard Detaille in 1891, based upon the cavalry charge of the French 4th Hussars during the Battle of Friedland. The actual battle had taken place on 14 June 1807, some 41 years before the artist's birth.","Vive L'Empereur (painting)"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}